      "content": "Even a single, unplanned dose increase carries risks that are not worth the gamble you're taking. Medications like Lisinopril require careful titration to ensure your body adjusts safely to the new level. Since you are experiencing concerning symptoms alongside high readings, the safest and most direct path is to call your provider's nurse line for immediate guidance. They can give you advice specific to your medical history while keeping you safe.",
